\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S6}{\ignorespaces The replay advantage co-occurs with training-pool donor provenance, but provenance and similarity remain confounded. (a) Donor-construction gaps relative to local REC: SEEN-PURE $+10.24$; UNSEEN-PURE $-4.27$ (paired-item CI $[-5.39,-3.20]$); the pool-substitution estimand $(\mathrm  {SEEN}-\mathrm  {REC})-(\mathrm  {UNSEEN}-\mathrm  {REC})=+14.51$; CROSSFIT pooled $-3.8$ (text only, no CI). (b) Balanced 605-query factorial: released evaluator (star) vs.\ six-reconstruction means (circles) for the pool-provenance and similarity main effects and their interaction. Donor-pool provenance contrast; not an identified training-exposure effect.\relax }}{19}{figure.caption.99}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s6_donor_origin}{{S6}{19}{The replay advantage co-occurs with training-pool donor provenance, but provenance and similarity remain confounded. (a) Donor-construction gaps relative to local REC: SEEN-PURE $+10.24$; UNSEEN-PURE $-4.27$ (paired-item CI $[-5.39,-3.20]$); the pool-substitution estimand $(\mathrm {SEEN}-\mathrm {REC})-(\mathrm {UNSEEN}-\mathrm {REC})=+14.51$; CROSSFIT pooled $-3.8$ (text only, no CI). (b) Balanced 605-query factorial: released evaluator (star) vs.\ six-reconstruction means (circles) for the pool-provenance and similarity main effects and their interaction. Donor-pool provenance contrast; not an identified training-exposure effect.\relax }{figure.caption.99}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S7}{\ignorespaces Adversarial unit-test response under the released evaluator and its absence across the canonical (clip$=$1.0) panel (relocated from the main text). (a) System scores (sacreBLEU-4, 641 queries): TN-PURE 23.02 vs.\ REC 12.78 ($\Delta {=}+10.24$, post-selected), with TN-PTCOMP 18.86, PT 1.59, oracle-gloss 11.4, random-donor 0.90 ($\pm $1 SD, 20 seeds). (b) Per-checkpoint gaps: released ($+10.24$) vs.\ fourteen legacy reconstructions, all negative (donor-cluster bootstrap CIs; dispersion $[-1.85,-0.80]$). The remaining families (full panel $[-2.80,-0.21]$) are in main Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:competence}; none is positive---an absence the main text (\S  \ref  {sec:sensitivity}) traces to the shared clip threshold (unclipped: $+11.19$).\relax }}{20}{figure.caption.145}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s7_headline}{{S7}{20}{Adversarial unit-test response under the released evaluator and its absence across the canonical (clip$=$1.0) panel (relocated from the main text). (a) System scores (sacreBLEU-4, 641 queries): TN-PURE 23.02 vs.\ REC 12.78 ($\Delta {=}+10.24$, post-selected), with TN-PTCOMP 18.86, PT 1.59, oracle-gloss 11.4, random-donor 0.90 ($\pm $1 SD, 20 seeds). (b) Per-checkpoint gaps: released ($+10.24$) vs.\ fourteen legacy reconstructions, all negative (donor-cluster bootstrap CIs; dispersion $[-1.85,-0.80]$). The remaining families (full panel $[-2.80,-0.21]$) are in main Fig.~\ref {fig:competence}; none is positive---an absence the main text (\S \ref {sec:sensitivity}) traces to the shared clip threshold (unclipped: $+11.19$).\relax }{figure.caption.145}{}}
