\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces Canonical checkpoint registry. 76 training runs across 12 families (disk-scanned; auto-generated from \texttt  {results/canonical\_checkpoint\_registry.json}). Of these 76 runs, 74 were beam-3 decoded on PHX-public under the canonical \S  \ref  {sec:retrieval} donor registry. The 74 decoded runs reduce to 73 unique weight binaries: the long-schedule seed-202 artifact is byte-identical to the validation-freq-misread seed-202 artifact (same wandb run, identical per-step losses, identical best-checkpoint SHA-256) and counts once. 69 non-degenerate decoded training runs enter the non-replication count (all 69 with strictly negative gaps; all share the clip$=$1.0 inference, resolved in Sup.\nobreakspace  {}U). Each family row's columns sum to the Total row.\relax }}{26}{table.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:checkpoint_registry}{{S4}{26}{Canonical checkpoint registry. 76 training runs across 12 families (disk-scanned; auto-generated from \texttt {results/canonical\_checkpoint\_registry.json}). Of these 76 runs, 74 were beam-3 decoded on PHX-public under the canonical \S \ref {sec:retrieval} donor registry. The 74 decoded runs reduce to 73 unique weight binaries: the long-schedule seed-202 artifact is byte-identical to the validation-freq-misread seed-202 artifact (same wandb run, identical per-step losses, identical best-checkpoint SHA-256) and counts once. 69 non-degenerate decoded training runs enter the non-replication count (all 69 with strictly negative gaps; all share the clip$=$1.0 inference, resolved in Sup.~U). Each family row's columns sum to the Total row.\relax }{table.caption.11}{}}
